# Copy to deploy/dev.secrets.env and fill in. Git-ignored, and no script ever writes it —
# which is the difference between this file and deploy/dev.local.env, the one scripts/tunnel.sh
# rewrites on every run. stack.sh layers both over dev.env.
#
# Nothing here is required. Without it the stack comes up and everything works except the
# AI features, which say what is missing.

# How the claude-bridge container signs in to Claude.
#
# The dev API has no Anthropic key, so it calls the bridge instead, and the bridge runs the
# `claude` CLI — which in a container has no Keychain to read a login from. Mint the token on
# your own machine, where you are already signed in:
#
#     claude setup-token
#
# It prints an sk-ant-oat… token. Paste it below, then `pnpm stack:dev`.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# An Anthropic API key instead, if you have one. In dev it still travels through the bridge —
# the CLI is run with it — so the AI features behave the same either way; a deployment, having
# no bridge, uses it directly.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
